Make the plugin managers discoverable on Drupal 12.

Drupal 12 dropped annotation-only plugin discovery, so a manager has to name
an attribute class. Passing the attribute alongside the existing annotation
selects AttributeDiscoveryWithAnnotations, which keeps every annotated plugin
webform ships working - the element plugins alone number over 100.

See https://www.drupal.org/node/3395582

diff --git a/src/Attribute/WebformElement.php b/src/Attribute/WebformElement.php
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/Attribute/WebformElement.php
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+<?php
+
+declare(strict_types=1);
+
+namespace Drupal\webform\Attribute;
+
+use Drupal\Component\Plugin\Attribute\Plugin;
+
+/**
+ * Defines a WebformElement attribute.
+ *
+ * Webform ships its element plugins with annotations, and naming this class
+ * alongside the annotation selects AttributeDiscoveryWithAnnotations, which
+ * reads both. It carries no properties of its own for that reason.
+ *
+ * Plugin Namespace: Plugin\WebformElement
+ *
+ * @see \Drupal\webform\Plugin\WebformElementManager
+ * @see \Drupal\webform\Annotation\WebformElement
+ * @see plugin_api
+ *
+ * @ingroup plugin_api
+ */
+#[\Attribute(\Attribute::TARGET_CLASS)]
+class WebformElement extends Plugin {
+
+}
